WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.009
'Sup homeslice!

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:14.620
This week we flying high with The Portrait
of the Artist as a Young Man by James Joyce.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.980
Aight, slick.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.720
Let's get something straight up in here.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.350
This book flowin' about one main thing: the
development of the artist, Stephen Dedalus.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.890
And we jumpin from one episode to another
as he grindin' through all sorts of sh*t from

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.510
his time as a young thug.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:35.800
At the start, we checkin his only memories
from the baby days: smells, sensations, and

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.500
a story his Pops once told him about a moo
cow.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.420
Hmmhmm.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.300
Later, Stephen gets sent to Clongowes Wood
College.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:48.179
And even though he just a little G gettin
schooled with other homies, he realize he

00:00:48.179 --> 00:00:50.339
ain't like the rest of these simple scrubs.

00:00:50.339 --> 00:00:53.870
But soon Stephen don't gotta go back to that
trap no more.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.260
His Daddy been acting a straight fool and
the family all outta that cash money.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.239
So the Dedalus crew high-tail it to Dublin,
and Stephen starts thuggin in a new school.

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:07.270
One night, Stephen starts wandering around
town and peeps a fine lil' number turning

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:13.340
tricks, so he throws her some dough and ends
up dippin his pen in more than just ink, nah

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.360
mean?

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.000
Yeah!

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.500
Stephen starts chasin' tail and rubbin' it
raw on the reg, until one day he hears some

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.300
tight ass preacher rhymin' about fire and
brimstone.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:28.180
Stephen just about sh*ts his pants and decides
it's time to hit that Bible HARDCORE.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:34.240
Our boy keepin' it so church that one of the
priests ask him to join up with his holy posse

00:01:34.249 --> 00:01:35.729
and enter the priesthood.

00:01:35.729 --> 00:01:40.130
Eventually, Stephen all like 'nah, priest
blood, but that ain't my style.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.049
Then one day while Stephen lurkin round the
beach, he catches a glimpse at one of the

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:46.500
finest asses he's ever seen.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.720
A ass so fine that it changes a brother's
life FOREVER.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.039
After that, he decide he gonna spread those
wings and create like a true blue artist with

00:01:56.039 --> 00:01:58.429
a free and proud soul.

00:01:58.429 --> 00:02:00.020
Like a boss.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:04.750
But all the cats he kickin' it with- family,
friends, religious peeps, they all just crampin'

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:05.799
his style.

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:14.670
So Stephen keeps it real and chucks up the
deuce to the world he know.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.319
Let me lay this game on you, B.

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:21.879
This book about a sensitive little G, comin
up in a family, religion, and country that

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:24.560
tryna drill a certain view of the world in
his head.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.470
But as he grow up, Steve-O decide he just
can't flow with that mess.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.360
Like Cranley say, Stephen wanted

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.760
And the only way to keep it that trill is
to throw up your middle finger to all that

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.200
sh*t that's holdin' you back.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.200
Now if you goin' hard in the paint, you gots
to peep Joyce's mad artistry up in here.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.920
See this sh*t right here is one of the first
books in which the motifs are the most important

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.220
element of the text.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.939
And Joyce flippin' them literary devices like
a mothaf*ckin' hustler.

00:02:55.939 --> 00:03:01.920
This cat packed just about all the novel's
images, motifs, and symbols in the first few

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.330
pages: daddies, roads, water, ladies, roses,
birds...

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.390
I could go on, playa!

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:12.080
Matta fact, some of this sh*t so similar to
old Jim Joyce's life that some cases think

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.280
this book is straight up autobiographical.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.959
And that Stephen reppin' Joyce himself.

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:22.599
See, like Stevie, Jimmy J had the balls to
stick it to his upbringing and define himself

00:03:22.599 --> 00:03:25.349
outside his country and religion.

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:30.140
Even though Stephen's story starts off with
his biological Daddy tryna school him by dropping

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:35.360
some verses about how the world be, our main
man ends up gettin learned by a different Pops,

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.740
the one he's named after...

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:47.060
Stephen actually goin' off about a character
in Greek myth named Daedalus, and Daedalus

00:03:47.069 --> 00:03:49.269
is one of the baddest mothers you ever seen.

00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:52.140
Fool could invent like nobody's business.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:57.010
Matta fact, he and his son, Icarus, actually
busted out of the slammer, by ghetto-riggin'

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:59.019
